{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>אל</b> — The meaning: every nation, when rejoicing comes to them, rejoices. It is fitting that not one of them commits harlotry against its god, as you did — you loved to give hire to the Baalim in place of the grain of your Elohim, and this is the harlotry. Therefore threshing-floor and winepress, for strangers shall devour them; he will deny them as though he does not know them."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:39.508901037Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}